==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-opt|pt}} {{term|temer|lang=roa-opt}}, {{etyl|la|pt}} {{term|timēre|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|timeō||I fear|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Paulista}} {{IPA|/te.ˈme(ɹ)/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|/te.ˈme(ɻ)/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/tɨ.ˈmeɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|te|mer|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|tem|er}}

# to [[fear]] {{gloss|to feel fear about something}}
# {{context|chiefly|theology|lang=pt}} to [[fear]] {{gloss|to venerate; to feel awe towards}}
# to be [[afraid]] {{gloss|regretful, sorry}}
#: '''Temo''' que não posso ajudar.
#:: '''I’m afraid''' I can’t help.

